  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nLab\na11y-probe\n\n// Tool\n\na11y-probe \n\nA command line check that tabs through your page and tells you where focus got lost.\n\nView the repo\nstars\n640\ndownloads\n8,900\nlicense\nMIT\nInstall\nCopy\nnpx a11y-probe https://your-site.com\n\n\nREADME.md\nMIT\n\na11y-probe opens your page in a headless browser, presses Tab until focus is back where it started and prints every stop: what was focused, whether you could see it, and the name a screen reader would announce.\n\nUsage\nbash\nCopy\nnpx a11y-probe https://your-site.com/checkout --width 390\n\n\n\n 1  a      \"Skip to content\"        ring ok\n\n 2  a      \"Northwind home\"         ring ok\n\n 3  button \"\"                       NO NAME\n\n 4  input  \"Card number\"            ring ok\n\n 5  div    (focus lost)             NOT VISIBLE\n\nWhat it catches\nControls with no accessible name\nFocus that lands on something invisible or off screen\nFocus traps, and menus you cannot leave with Escape\n\nIt exits with code 1 when anything fails, so it can sit in CI next to your tests.\n\nIn this readme\n\n01\nUsage\n02\nWhat it catches\nKind\nTool\nLicense\nMIT\nRepository\ngithub.com\nMore from the lab. \n06\nEverything in the lab\nTool · 410 stars\ntokens-to-css\nTurns a design token file into typed CSS custom properties, with dark mode built in.\nExperiment · 320 stars\nshader-notes\nForty small WebGL sketches, each one under fifty lines and explained line by line.\nLibrary · 2,140 stars\nuse-latency\nA React hook that measures how long every interaction really takes, in production.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
